IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `er5-pilot-weeks`

-- Tests of er5-pilot-weeks (regs 77.2, 77.3 to 77.6, 77.91, 77.92, 77.992 and 77.993). Expected values are written by hand from the text of the Regulations
-- (SOR-96-332.txt lines 1433-1441, 1469-1494 and 1578-1596), beside each assertion, before the run. Calendar facts (which day of the week a date is, 364 days before a date) were
-- checked against Python's datetime, not against the encoding. The weeks the Schedule II.2, II.7 and II.93 tables give (45 and 52 below) are invented for the test: the tables are piece er6's.

§ `Reg 77.2 - Pilot Project No. 6 (src:1433-1441)`

#ASSERT `reg 77.2(1) the purpose of Pilot Project No. 6` EQUALS "assessing the costs and impact of increasing weeks of benefits in selected economic regions"
-- The period of establishment runs from June 6, 2004 to June 4, 2006, both days included.
#ASSERT `reg 77.2(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 6` (YearMonthDay 2004 6 6) TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 77.2(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 6` (YearMonthDay 2006 6 4) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.2(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 6` (YearMonthDay 2004 6 5) TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.2(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 6` (YearMonthDay 2006 6 5) TRUE)
-- Not resident in a region of Schedule II.1.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.2(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 6` (YearMonthDay 2005 1 1) FALSE)
-- (3): an included claimant takes the weeks the table gives; others are left to s 12(2) of the Act (NOTHING here).
#ASSERT `reg 77.2(3) the maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid in the benefit period` TRUE 45 EQUALS JUST 45
#ASSERT `reg 77.2(3) the maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid in the benefit period` FALSE 45 EQUALS NOTHING
-- Regs 77.3 to 77.6: a stub that evaluates to the inert TRUE of a string chain.
#ASSERT `regs 77.3 to 77.6 are repealed and therefore not encoded`

§ `Reg 77.91 - Pilot Project No. 14 (src:1469-1484)`

#ASSERT `reg 77.91(1) the purpose of Pilot Project No. 14` EQUALS "assessing whether the extension of the number of weeks of benefits paid to a qualified claimant who undertakes long-term training encourages the claimant to pursue such training and improves their re-employability"

-- (3). The argument order is: the day the benefit period begins; years of 30% contributions among the 10; weeks of regular benefits in the 260 weeks; the day the return to work action plan became active, if it has;
-- referred under paragraph 25(1)(a); the course is full-time; its duration in weeks; the day it begins.
-- The benefit period begins on Sunday January 25, 2009. Every criterion met: 7 of 10 years; 35 weeks; plan active June 14, 2009 (exactly 20 weeks after); a full-time course of 20 weeks beginning May 31, 2009.
#ASSERT `reg 77.91(3) the claimant meets the criteria of Pilot Project No. 14` (YearMonthDay 2009 1 25) 7 35 (JUST (YearMonthDay 2009 6 14)) TRUE TRUE 20 (YearMonthDay 2009 5 31)
-- (a): only 6 of the 10 years.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.91(3) the claimant meets the criteria of Pilot Project No. 14` (YearMonthDay 2009 1 25) 6 35 (JUST (YearMonthDay 2009 6 14)) TRUE TRUE 20 (YearMonthDay 2009 5 31))
-- (b): 36 weeks is not less than 36.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.91(3) the claimant meets the criteria of Pilot Project No. 14` (YearMonthDay 2009 1 25) 7 36 (JUST (YearMonthDay 2009 6 14)) TRUE TRUE 20 (YearMonthDay 2009 5 31))
-- (c): a plan that became active on June 15, 2009, a day after the 20 weeks, but before August 23, 2009, for a benefit period that began before May 31, 2009: counts.
#ASSERT `reg 77.91(3) the claimant meets the criteria of Pilot Project No. 14` (YearMonthDay 2009 1 25) 7 35 (JUST (YearMonthDay 2009 6 15)) TRUE TRUE 20 (YearMonthDay 2009 5 31)
#ASSERT `reg 77.91(3) the claimant meets the criteria of Pilot Project No. 14` (YearMonthDay 2009 1 25) 7 35 (JUST (YearMonthDay 2009 8 22)) TRUE TRUE 20 (YearMonthDay 2009 5 31)
-- (c): on August 23, 2009 itself the second alternative is not met ("before August 23"), and the 20 weeks ended on June 14, 2009.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.91(3) the claimant meets the criteria of Pilot Project No. 14` (YearMonthDay 2009 1 25) 7 35 (JUST (YearMonthDay 2009 8 23)) TRUE TRUE 20 (YearMonthDay 2009 5 31))
-- (c): no active plan at all.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.91(3) the claimant meets the criteria of Pilot Project No. 14` (YearMonthDay 2009 1 25) 7 35 NOTHING TRUE TRUE 20 (YearMonthDay 2009 5 31))
-- (c): a benefit period beginning on Sunday May 31, 2009 did not begin "before May 31, 2009", so only the 20 weeks (to October 18, 2009) count.
#ASSERT `reg 77.91(3) the claimant meets the criteria of Pilot Project No. 14` (YearMonthDay 2009 5 31) 7 35 (JUST (YearMonthDay 2009 10 18)) TRUE TRUE 20 (YearMonthDay 2009 6 7)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.91(3) the claimant meets the criteria of Pilot Project No. 14` (YearMonthDay 2009 5 31) 7 35 (JUST (YearMonthDay 2009 10 19)) TRUE TRUE 20 (YearMonthDay 2009 6 7))
-- (d): not referred; not full-time; 19 weeks.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.91(3) the claimant meets the criteria of Pilot Project No. 14` (YearMonthDay 2009 1 25) 7 35 (JUST (YearMonthDay 2009 6 14)) FALSE TRUE 20 (YearMonthDay 2009 5 31))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.91(3) the claimant meets the criteria of Pilot Project No. 14` (YearMonthDay 2009 1 25) 7 35 (JUST (YearMonthDay 2009 6 14)) TRUE FALSE 20 (YearMonthDay 2009 5 31))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.91(3) the claimant meets the criteria of Pilot Project No. 14` (YearMonthDay 2009 1 25) 7 35 (JUST (YearMonthDay 2009 6 14)) TRUE TRUE 19 (YearMonthDay 2009 5 31))
-- (d)(iii): the course begins May 30, 2009, a day before the earliest date allowed.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.91(3) the claimant meets the criteria of Pilot Project No. 14` (YearMonthDay 2009 1 25) 7 35 (JUST (YearMonthDay 2009 6 14)) TRUE TRUE 20 (YearMonthDay 2009 5 30))
-- (d)(iii): the 52 weeks that start with January 25, 2009 end on January 23, 2010.
#ASSERT `reg 77.91(3) the claimant meets the criteria of Pilot Project No. 14` (YearMonthDay 2009 1 25) 7 35 (JUST (YearMonthDay 2009 6 14)) TRUE TRUE 20 (YearMonthDay 2010 1 23)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.91(3) the claimant meets the criteria of Pilot Project No. 14` (YearMonthDay 2009 1 25) 7 35 (JUST (YearMonthDay 2009 6 14)) TRUE TRUE 20 (YearMonthDay 2010 1 24))

-- (2): the benefit period is established in the period from January 25, 2009 to May 29, 2010, and the criteria are met.
#ASSERT `reg 77.91(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 14` (YearMonthDay 2009 1 25) TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 77.91(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 14` (YearMonthDay 2010 5 29) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.91(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 14` (YearMonthDay 2009 1 24) TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.91(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 14` (YearMonthDay 2010 5 30) TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.91(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 14` (YearMonthDay 2009 7 1) FALSE)

-- (6): one week for every five weeks completed, at most 12.
#ASSERT `reg 77.91(6) the period granted for job-search purposes, in weeks` 25 EQUALS 5
#ASSERT `reg 77.91(6) the period granted for job-search purposes, in weeks` 24 EQUALS 4
#ASSERT `reg 77.91(6) the period granted for job-search purposes, in weeks` 4 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `reg 77.91(6) the period granted for job-search purposes, in weeks` 59 EQUALS 11
#ASSERT `reg 77.91(6) the period granted for job-search purposes, in weeks` 60 EQUALS 12
#ASSERT `reg 77.91(6) the period granted for job-search purposes, in weeks` 61 EQUALS 12
#ASSERT `reg 77.91(6) the period granted for job-search purposes, in weeks` 100 EQUALS 12
-- The period begins on the Sunday after the last day of attendance: after Wednesday September 2, 2009 and after Saturday September 5, 2009 it is Sunday September 6; after that Sunday it is September 13.
#ASSERT `reg 77.91(6) the Sunday on which the period granted for job-search purposes begins` (YearMonthDay 2009 9 2) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2009 9 6
#ASSERT `reg 77.91(6) the Sunday on which the period granted for job-search purposes begins` (YearMonthDay 2009 9 5) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2009 9 6
#ASSERT `reg 77.91(6) the Sunday on which the period granted for job-search purposes begins` (YearMonthDay 2009 9 6) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2009 9 13

-- (4): the extension is the course and the job-search weeks, at most 104; an included claimant only.
#ASSERT `reg 77.91(4) the number of weeks by which the benefit period is extended` TRUE 30 6 EQUALS 36
#ASSERT `reg 77.91(4) the number of weeks by which the benefit period is extended` TRUE 92 12 EQUALS 104
#ASSERT `reg 77.91(4) the number of weeks by which the benefit period is extended` TRUE 93 12 EQUALS 104
#ASSERT `reg 77.91(4) the number of weeks by which the benefit period is extended` TRUE 100 12 EQUALS 104
#ASSERT `reg 77.91(4) the number of weeks by which the benefit period is extended` FALSE 30 6 EQUALS 0

-- (7): when a ground to terminate the referral exists, (5) ceases to apply on the Sunday after the last day of attendance.
#ASSERT `reg 77.91(7) the Sunday on which subsection 77.91(5) ceases to apply` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2009 9 2) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2009 9 6)
#ASSERT `reg 77.91(7) the Sunday on which subsection 77.91(5) ceases to apply` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2009 9 2) EQUALS NOTHING

-- (5): the argument order is: included; the weeks the Act gives; the extra weeks in the extended benefit period; (5) has ceased to apply.
#ASSERT `reg 77.91(5) the maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid` TRUE 26 10 FALSE EQUALS 36
#ASSERT `reg 77.91(5) the maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid` TRUE 26 10 TRUE EQUALS 26
#ASSERT `reg 77.91(5) the maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid` FALSE 26 10 FALSE EQUALS 26

§ `Reg 77.92 - Pilot Project No. 15 (src:1487-1494)`

#ASSERT `reg 77.92(1) the purpose of Pilot Project No. 15` EQUALS "assessing the costs and impact of extending the number of weeks of benefits in selected economic regions"

-- The second Saturday after a day. January 1, 2011 was a Saturday; January 2 a Sunday; January 8 a Saturday.
#ASSERT `er5 reg 77.92 the second Saturday after the day` (YearMonthDay 2011 1 2) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2011 1 15
#ASSERT `er5 reg 77.92 the second Saturday after the day` (YearMonthDay 2011 1 3) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2011 1 15
#ASSERT `er5 reg 77.92 the second Saturday after the day` (YearMonthDay 2011 1 7) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2011 1 15
-- After a Saturday itself, the first Saturday after is the next one, so the second is a week later again.
#ASSERT `er5 reg 77.92 the second Saturday after the day` (YearMonthDay 2011 1 8) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2011 1 22
#ASSERT `er5 reg 77.92 the second Saturday after the day` (YearMonthDay 2011 1 1) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2011 1 15

-- (2)(b): (i) the rate below 8.0% for 12 consecutive periods, the 12th beginning Sunday January 2, 2011: the last day is Saturday January 15, 2011; (ii) any other case: September 15, 2012.
#ASSERT `reg 77.92(2)(b) the last day on which a benefit period can be established under Pilot Project No. 15` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2011 1 2) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2011 1 15
#ASSERT `reg 77.92(2)(b) the last day on which a benefit period can be established under Pilot Project No. 15` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2011 1 2) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2012 9 15
-- (2): the argument order is: resident in a region of Schedule II.6; the day the benefit period is established; the last day for establishing.
#ASSERT `reg 77.92(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 15` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2010 9 12) (YearMonthDay 2012 9 15)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.92(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 15` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2010 9 11) (YearMonthDay 2012 9 15))
#ASSERT `reg 77.92(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 15` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2012 9 15) (YearMonthDay 2012 9 15)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.92(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 15` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2012 9 16) (YearMonthDay 2012 9 15))
-- With the end brought forward to January 15, 2011 by (2)(b)(i).
#ASSERT `reg 77.92(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 15` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2011 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2011 1 15)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.92(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 15` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2011 1 16) (YearMonthDay 2011 1 15))
-- Not resident in a region of Schedule II.6.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.92(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 15` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2011 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2012 9 15))
-- (3): the notice is owed when (2)(b)(i) is satisfied.
#ASSERT `reg 77.92(3) the Commission must publish a notice in the Canada Gazette and on its website` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.92(3) the Commission must publish a notice in the Canada Gazette and on its website` FALSE)
-- (4): the weeks of Schedule II.7 (52 here, invented) for an included claimant.
#ASSERT `reg 77.92(4) the maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid in the benefit period` TRUE 52 EQUALS JUST 52
#ASSERT `reg 77.92(4) the maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid in the benefit period` FALSE 52 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Reg 77.992 - Pilot Project No. 21 (src:1578-1591)`

#ASSERT `reg 77.992(1) the purpose of Pilot Project No. 21` EQUALS "testing the effectiveness of a mechanism that targets persons who meet the criteria set out in subsection (2) and testing the outcomes of increasing the number of weeks of benefits paid to the targeted population"

-- (4). The first week of the benefit period begins Sunday September 1, 2019. The weeks 52, 104, 156, 208 and 260 before it begin on Sundays 2018-09-02, 2017-09-03, 2016-09-04, 2015-09-06 and 2014-09-07;
-- each period runs from 56 days before that Sunday to 62 days after it (the end of the eighth week after).
-- The argument order is: the Sunday that begins the first week; the day the earlier benefit period began.
#ASSERT `reg 77.992(4) the earlier benefit period is considered to have begun around the same time of year` (YearMonthDay 2019 9 1) (YearMonthDay 2018 9 2)
-- The edges of the 52-week period: July 8, 2018 and November 3, 2018.
#ASSERT `reg 77.992(4) the earlier benefit period is considered to have begun around the same time of year` (YearMonthDay 2019 9 1) (YearMonthDay 2018 7 8)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.992(4) the earlier benefit period is considered to have begun around the same time of year` (YearMonthDay 2019 9 1) (YearMonthDay 2018 7 7))
#ASSERT `reg 77.992(4) the earlier benefit period is considered to have begun around the same time of year` (YearMonthDay 2019 9 1) (YearMonthDay 2018 11 3)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.992(4) the earlier benefit period is considered to have begun around the same time of year` (YearMonthDay 2019 9 1) (YearMonthDay 2018 11 4))
-- (b) to (e): one day in the 104-, 156-, 208- and 260-week periods, and the edge days of the 260-week period (July 13 and November 8, 2014).
#ASSERT `reg 77.992(4) the earlier benefit period is considered to have begun around the same time of year` (YearMonthDay 2019 9 1) (YearMonthDay 2017 9 3)
#ASSERT `reg 77.992(4) the earlier benefit period is considered to have begun around the same time of year` (YearMonthDay 2019 9 1) (YearMonthDay 2016 9 4)
#ASSERT `reg 77.992(4) the earlier benefit period is considered to have begun around the same time of year` (YearMonthDay 2019 9 1) (YearMonthDay 2015 9 6)
#ASSERT `reg 77.992(4) the earlier benefit period is considered to have begun around the same time of year` (YearMonthDay 2019 9 1) (YearMonthDay 2014 7 13)
#ASSERT `reg 77.992(4) the earlier benefit period is considered to have begun around the same time of year` (YearMonthDay 2019 9 1) (YearMonthDay 2014 11 8)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.992(4) the earlier benefit period is considered to have begun around the same time of year` (YearMonthDay 2019 9 1) (YearMonthDay 2014 11 9))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.992(4) the earlier benefit period is considered to have begun around the same time of year` (YearMonthDay 2019 9 1) (YearMonthDay 2014 7 12))
-- A benefit period that began in the middle of the year: February 3, 2018 is in none of the five periods.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.992(4) the earlier benefit period is considered to have begun around the same time of year` (YearMonthDay 2019 9 1) (YearMonthDay 2018 2 4))

-- (3). The 260 weeks before the benefit period begin on Sunday September 7, 2014 (260 times seven days before September 1, 2019).
-- The argument order is: the Sunday that begins the first week; the day the earlier benefit period was established; a notification received for a week in the 260-week period.
#ASSERT `reg 77.992(3) the earlier benefit period is considered to have been established within the 260-week period` (YearMonthDay 2019 9 1) (YearMonthDay 2014 9 7) FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.992(3) the earlier benefit period is considered to have been established within the 260-week period` (YearMonthDay 2019 9 1) (YearMonthDay 2014 9 6) FALSE)
-- Established before the 260 weeks, but a notification was received for a week inside them.
#ASSERT `reg 77.992(3) the earlier benefit period is considered to have been established within the 260-week period` (YearMonthDay 2019 9 1) (YearMonthDay 2014 9 6) TRUE
-- Established after the benefit period began: not an earlier one.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.992(3) the earlier benefit period is considered to have been established within the 260-week period` (YearMonthDay 2019 9 1) (YearMonthDay 2019 9 8) TRUE)

-- (2)(c) and (d): counts.
#ASSERT `reg 77.992(2)(c) at least three benefit periods had been established` 3
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.992(2)(c) at least three benefit periods had been established` 2)
#ASSERT `reg 77.992(2)(d) at least two of those benefit periods had begun around the same time of year` 2
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.992(2)(d) at least two of those benefit periods had begun around the same time of year` 1)
-- (2): the argument order is: the day the benefit period is established; resident in a region of Schedule II.92; (c); (d).
#ASSERT `reg 77.992(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 21` (YearMonthDay 2018 8 5) TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.992(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 21` (YearMonthDay 2018 8 4) TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `reg 77.992(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 21` (YearMonthDay 2021 9 25) TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.992(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 21` (YearMonthDay 2021 9 26) TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.992(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 21` (YearMonthDay 2019 9 1) FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.992(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 21` (YearMonthDay 2019 9 1) TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.992(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 21` (YearMonthDay 2019 9 1) TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- (5): the weeks of Schedule II.93 (52 here, invented) for an included claimant.
#ASSERT `reg 77.992(5) the maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid in the benefit period` TRUE 52 EQUALS JUST 52
#ASSERT `reg 77.992(5) the maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid in the benefit period` FALSE 52 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Reg 77.993 - Pilot Project No. 22 (src:1594-1596)`

#ASSERT `reg 77.993(1) the purpose of Pilot Project No. 22` EQUALS "testing whether certain claimants who meet the conditions set out in subsection 12(2.3) of the Act require more additional weeks of benefits as a result of low unemployment rates"
#ASSERT `reg 77.993(3) the schedule that is read in place of Schedule V in subsection 12(2.3) of the Act` EQUALS "Schedule II.94 of the Employment Insurance Regulations"
-- The period of establishment runs from September 10, 2023 to September 7, 2024, both days included.
#ASSERT `reg 77.993(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 22` (YearMonthDay 2023 9 10) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.993(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 22` (YearMonthDay 2023 9 9) TRUE)
#ASSERT `reg 77.993(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 22` (YearMonthDay 2024 9 7) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.993(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 22` (YearMonthDay 2024 9 8) TRUE)
-- The conditions of s 12(2.3) are not met.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.993(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 22` (YearMonthDay 2024 1 1) FALSE)
